From c806d37b9e83cdee0574abd1fb47f0675372a9fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marie-222 <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:51:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] desktop-shell: add xdg-activation-v1, and tell msrdc about
 the z order change

A Wayland client cannot raise one of its own windows by itself: it needs
xdg-activation-v1, which this compositor did not offer. winit's
Window::focus_window() therefore did nothing (Neovide could not move the focus
to another of its windows).

Add the global. A client gets a token with get_activation_token + commit, and
activate(token, surface) raises the surface the way a click on its window from
the Windows side does (shell_backend_request_window_activate()). Only tokens
handed out here are accepted, each one once and for 30 seconds. The serial,
app_id and surface given to the token request are not checked; they only pick
the seat.

notify_window_zorder_change() of the RDP backend had no caller, so a z order
change made inside Weston was never sent to the RDP client, and msrdc kept the
old window in front. Call it after an activation.
---
